    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That feels a bit like a semantic distinction rather than a technical one. \"Redistributing power\" and \"adjusting power allocation\" sound like two different ways of describing the exact same process. An examiner is going to see right through that \"load-shifting topology\" tag if we can't point to a specific mechanism that makes it work.\n\nIs there a specific component or a protocol-level difference in how the impedance is actually handled? For example, is there a difference in the sampling frequency, the type of signal being processed, or a specific hardware interface used in our client's mechanism that isn't present in the 2018 patent? I need a hard engineering fact we can point to, not just a different way of phrasing the same concept.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
